# Prerequisites

- **Helm 4** (Helm 3 is no longer supported), `kubectl` and `helm-docs`. They are pinned in [mise.toml](../mise.toml) and installed with `make install-deps` (see [REQUIREMENTS.md](../REQUIREMENTS.md)).
- Kubernetes {{ template "chart.kubeVersion" . }}.

# Makefile shortcuts

Run `make help` inside `helm-chart/` to list every target. The most used ones:

| Target | What it does |
|--------|--------------|
| `make lint` | `helm lint --strict .` |
| `make template` | Renders the manifests locally |
| `make dry-run` | Server-side dry-run against the current cluster |
| `make install` | `helm upgrade --install` (waits for the pods) |
| `make uninstall` | Removes the release |
| `make gen-docs` | Regenerates this README from `values.yaml` |

Use `RELEASE=<name>` and `NAMESPACE=<ns>` to change the defaults (`gofipe`/`gofipe`).

# Installing the Chart

- Access a Kubernetes cluster.

- Change the values according to the need of the environment in ``{{ template "chart.name" . }}/values.yaml`` file. The [Parameters](#parameters) section lists the parameters that can be configured during installation.

- Test the installation with command:

```bash
helm upgrade --install {{ template "chart.name" . }} -f {{ template "chart.name" . }}/values.yaml {{ template "chart.name" . }}/ -n {{ template "chart.name" . }} --create-namespace --dry-run=server
```

- To install/upgrade the chart with the release name `{{ template "chart.name" . }}`:

```bash
helm upgrade --install {{ template "chart.name" . }} -f {{ template "chart.name" . }}/values.yaml {{ template "chart.name" . }}/ -n {{ template "chart.name" . }} --create-namespace
```

Create a port-forward with the follow command:

```bash
kubectl port-forward svc/{{ template "chart.name" . }} 8080:80 -n {{ template "chart.name" . }}
```

Open the browser and access the URL: http://localhost:8080

## Uninstalling the Chart

To uninstall/delete the `{{ template "chart.name" . }}` deployment:

```bash
helm uninstall {{ template "chart.name" . }} -n {{ template "chart.name" . }}
```

The command removes all the Kubernetes components associated with the chart and deletes the release.

